# Most maintainers build with `cargo`; Docker is for prod/CI. This file
# exists primarily as a *safety net* so a future `COPY . .` in the
# Dockerfile can't accidentally pull `data/.ryokan-key` (the AEAD key
# for OAuth-token encryption) or `data/ryokan.db` (the live SQLite DB)
# into image layers that ship to GHCR. Build-context size is the
# secondary win — `target/` alone can be hundreds of GB.

# Cargo build artifacts.
target/

# Local SQLite database, artwork blob cache, AEAD key, and any sentinel
# files. The `RYOKAN_ENCRYPTION_KEY` fallback at `data/.ryokan-key`
# (raw 32 bytes, mode 0600) MUST NOT enter image layers.
data/
# The same files when they live outside data/: `RYOKAN_DATA_DIR` /
# `RYOKAN_KEY_FILE_PATH` can move them, and `--sanitize-db-for-debug`
# writes `ryokan-sanitized.db` to the working directory.
**/.ryokan-key
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.db-journal

# Git history (the runtime image doesn't need it).
.git/
.gitignore

# Local mutation-testing artifacts (outputs, run logs, and the weekly
# report script's baseline and report).
mutants.out*/
mutants-*.log
mutants.baseline*.json
mutants-report*.md

# Editor / IDE / OS clutter.
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store

# Claude Code workspace settings — agents/ and skills/ live here but
# aren't needed in the image. The repo's .gitignore already shares the
# subset that ships in git.
.claude/

# Documentation and CI configs aren't compiled into the binary.
.github/
*.md
!README.md
# MkDocs source — published to GH Pages, not shipped in the image.
docs/
mkdocs.yml
docs-requirements.in
docs-requirements.txt
# The built docs site and Zensical's cache.
site/
.cache/

# Build/dev tooling not needed in the image. `.cargo/` pins clang +
# mold, which the builder image doesn't have.
.cargo/
.config/
.env
.env.*
.venv*/
# The Noto Sans JP source font scripts/subset-noto-sans-jp.py downloads.
NotoSansJP*.ttf

# Tests + fixtures are excluded from the binary build (they're
# integration test crates gated by `--features test-support`).
# Keeping them out of the build context shaves the upload further.
tests/
